-- title:
--   Prime-to-p torsion: nodal-principal reduction forces principality
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be an algebraically closed field, $A \subseteq L$ a valuation subring, $\pi$ a nonzero element of the maximal ideal of $A$, and assume $A$ has rank one in the form: for every nonzero $x \in L$ and every $y$ in the maximal ideal there is $n$ with $A$-valuation of $y^n$ at most that of $x$. Let $F$ be a field extension of $L$, let $n, m$ be natural numbers, and let $\bar F_i$ ($i \in \mathrm{Fin}\,n$) be fields over the residue field $\kappa$ of $A$, all of whose places over $\kappa$ are rational (the residue field of each place is generated by $\kappa$). Assume given component charts $C_i$ of $F$ over $\bar F_i$ relative to $A$, with all places in $(C_i).\mathrm{dom}$ rational; annuli $\mathrm{An}_e, \mathrm{An}'_e$ ($e \in \mathrm{Fin}\,m$) with edge data $\mathrm{src}, \mathrm{tgt}$ and node places $x_s(e)$ of $\bar F_{\mathrm{src}(e)}$, $x_t(e)$ of $\bar F_{\mathrm{tgt}(e)}$, and weights $w_e$. The hypotheses on this data are: each pair $\mathrm{An}'_e, \mathrm{An}_e$ has the same domain and the same modulus, the modulus is nonzero in $L$, and the product of the two parameters is the image of that modulus; the modulus of $\mathrm{An}_e$ is a unit times $\pi^{w_e}$; $\mathrm{An}_e$ is attached to $C_{\mathrm{src}(e)}$ at $x_s(e)$ and $\mathrm{An}'_e$ to $C_{\mathrm{tgt}(e)}$ at $x_t(e)$; every node of every chart is an endpoint of some edge, and the endpoint assignment $\mathrm{Fin}\,m \oplus \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \Sigma_j\,\mathrm{Place}(\kappa, \bar F_j)$ is injective over each node; every place of $F$ over $L$ lies either in exactly one chart domain and in no annulus, or in exactly one annulus domain and in no chart domain; a disc-fibre condition, namely for each non-node place $Q$ of $\bar F_i$ there is $T$ in the integers of $C_i$ whose residue is nonzero and has order $1$ at $Q$, such that $T$ lies in the valuation ring of every place $P$ of $(C_i).\mathrm{dom}$ above $Q$ with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,T$ in the maximal ideal of $A$, and such that each $c$ in the maximal ideal of $A$ is $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,T$ for exactly one place $P$ above $Q$; and the genus identity $\mathrm{genusFF}(L, F) + n = \sum_i \mathrm{genusFF}(\kappa, \bar F_i) + m + 1$. Assume further that $F/L$ and each $\bar F_i/\kappa$ are curves with essentially finite type, that $M$ is a semistable model for this data and $D$ a descent of $M$, and that $k$ is a natural number whose image in $\kappa$ is a unit. Finally, let $D_i$ be divisors of $F$ over $L$ with $D_i$ supported in $(C_i).\mathrm{dom}$ and $\deg D_i = 0$, such that the tuple of push-forwards $(C_i)_*D_i$ along $(C_i).\mathrm{placeMap}$ is nodal principal, that is, there are nonzero $g_i \in \bar F_i$ and units $a_e \in \kappa^\times$ with $((C_i)_*D_i)(v) = v.\mathrm{ord}(g_i)$ for all places $v$ of $\bar F_i$ and, for each edge $e$, both $x_s(e)$ and $x_t(e)$ taking the value $a_e$ on $g_{\mathrm{src}(e)}$ and $g_{\mathrm{tgt}(e)}$ respectively; and such that $k \cdot \sum_i D_i$ is principal. The conclusion is that $\sum_i D_i$ is itself principal, that is, equal to the divisor of some nonzero element of $F$.
--
--   This is the injectivity of reduction on prime-to-$p$ torsion for the semistable situation: a degree-zero class supported on the chart domains whose reduction is trivial in the Picard group of the nodal special fibre, and a multiple of which by $k$ invertible in the residue field is trivial, is itself trivial. It feeds the counting bound [`AlgebraicCurve.natCard_torsion_tropicalPositionZero_mul_pow_le_of_semistableCovering_of_discFibres_of_rankOne_of_charZero_of_semistableModel`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.natCard_torsion_tropicalPositionZero_mul_pow_le_of_semistableCovering_of_discFibres_of_rankOne_of_charZero_of_semistableModel), which bounds the torsion of the degree-zero part in terms of the combinatorics of the special fibre.
